---
/**
 * The idea behind the studio, stated plainly. Leads with the outcome (a brand
 * worth returning to); the tooling never opens. The commerce motif carries the
 * section: every choice should earn its place on the shelf.
 */
---

<section class="f-section f-manifesto">
  <p class="f-label" data-f-fade>01 · The idea</p>

  <h2 class="f-statement f-display" data-f-lines>
    <span class="f-mask"><span class="f-mask-inner">Make it worth</span></span>
    <span class="f-mask"><span class="f-mask-inner">coming back for.</span></span>
  </h2>

  <div class="f-manifesto-cols">
    <p data-f-fade>
      A storefront is judged in seconds. We start from the moment a visitor
      lands and work backwards: what they need to see, feel, and trust before
      they reach for their card, agreed in plain language first.
    </p>
    <p data-f-fade>
      From there it is fast and tactile. Real screens you can click, vivid where
      it sells and quiet where it should, built to load quickly and hold up long
      after the launch-day rush.
    </p>
  </div>

  <span class="f-rule" data-f-rule aria-hidden="true"></span>
</section>

<style>
  .f-manifesto-cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    max-width: 920px;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.6rem, 7vh, 4rem);
  }
  .f-manifesto-cols p {
    max-width: 44ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.3vw, 1.14rem);
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--f-muted);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .f-manifesto-cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
